<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened runtime entitlements for Seedwell: none.

  Seedwell is not sandboxed (SPEC 12 #19: watch folders, library organizing, the agent socket), so the
  network entitlements (com.apple.security.network.client/server) and user-selected files only exist
  inside a sandbox and would do nothing here. Outgoing and incoming peer, tracker, DHT and uTP traffic
  and every file access work under the hardened runtime as is.

  Not needed, so not granted: JIT / unsigned executable memory (the Rust allocator maps anonymous
  non-executable pages), DYLD environment variables, Apple events, camera, microphone, contacts.
  Library validation stays ON: the only library loaded from outside is Sparkle.framework, signed with
  the same identity as the app. (Ad-hoc builds have no team id, so sign.sh adds
  disable-library-validation to those only; they are not distributable.)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
